  "intro": {
    "etiqueta": "Vehicle history",
    "titulo": "A documented <br/><strong> chapter of the <br/>RUF legacy.</strong>",
    "parrafos": [
      "Originally delivered in 2007 through <strong>Porsche Zentrum Essen</strong>, this 911 Carrera 4S, 997 generation, began its journey as a sophisticated Gran Turismo in <strong>Meteor Gray Metallic (LM7W)</strong> with a <strong>Classic Dark Brown</strong> leather interior.",
      "In 2011, with only <strong>12.234 km</strong> on the odometer, its first owner sent the car to the <strong>RUF Automobile facility in Pfaffenhausen</strong> for a comprehensive conversion to the <strong>Kompressor R</strong> specification. This transformation, with a cost of <strong>55.000 €</strong>, is meticulously documented by the original RUF invoice.",
      "The car retains its original chassis number from Porsche. The <strong>original VIN</strong>."
    ],
    "cita": "It's not just a prepared Porsche. It is a documented RUF conversion, carried out in Pfaffenhausen and retaining its original Porsche VIN.",
